        ("iGOT Karmayogi and the output against outcome distinction", "iGOT Karmayogi is the integrated government online training platform that delivers role-based modules at scale, and the exam-safe discipline is that enrolment, course counts, completion certificates and platform totals are outputs carried on a continuously updated dashboard whereas the outcome is demonstrated workplace application, which is why no learner count, course count, completion total, certificate figure, State memorandum count or training-institute accreditation figure is asserted anywhere in this package."),
        ("The Karmayogi Competency Model and the untested link", "The Karmayogi Competency Model maps behavioural, functional and domain competencies to specific roles and thereby makes the word competency operational rather than rhetorical, but the untested link in the entire reform is whether assessed competency actually governs posting decisions, because a competency framework that never enters the posting file changes training without changing allocation."),
        ("Generalist and specialist as a capacity-allocation problem", "The generalist and specialist question is best treated as a capacity-allocation problem rather than an either-or contest, because policy complexity in technology, finance and climate argues for specialist depth while administrative coordination across sectors and levels of government argues for generalist breadth, and competency mapping is precisely an attempt to allocate the right mix to each specific post instead of resolving the debate wholesale in either direction."),
        ("Lateral entry as a bounded supplement", "Lateral entry is the direct recruitment of domain experts from outside the regular cadre into specified senior positions at Joint Secretary, Director or Deputy Secretary level in selected ministries, and it operates as a periodic and targeted supplement to regular cadre promotion rather than a continuous or cadre-replacing channel; a lateral entrant typically serves a fixed and often shorter contractual tenure and may lack socialisation into permanent-service norms, so the genuine design question is whether it dilutes or complements the classical structural safeguards."),
        ("How neutrality erodes through posting and transfer discretion", "Neutrality erodes through an identifiable chain in which unconstrained posting and transfer discretion leads officers to anticipate the political executive's preference, advice is shaped before it is asked for, permanence protects the office rather than the post because dismissal is hard while displacement to an inconsequential post is easy, anonymity becomes asymmetric as the officer is publicly blamed in controversy and publicly invisible in achievement, and the resulting perception of partiality erodes the legitimacy of unelected discretion."),
        ("The protections that hold neutrality in place", "The protections against that chain are a transparent transfer and posting process, minimum-tenure norms, written reasons for any deviation, recorded advice, a functioning appraisal with meaningful differentiation and institutional rather than personal accountability for outcomes, and stating them as a connected set is what converts a description of politicisation into a reform answer that answers the directive."),
        ("The reciprocal obligation on the political executive", "The Doctrine of Democratic Governance implies a reciprocal obligation, because civil servants must act with integrity while political executives must equally refrain from politically motivated transfers and from pressure for partisan compliance that make neutral service impossible to sustain or to perceive, and a one-sided answer that only asks civil servants to improve misses the two-sided institutional design point the demand rewards."),
